ath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T17:16:33-07:00","id":1488227,"title":"","content":"Well Yes and no I've bin the the web page it's not complete though in my mind, like Chicago by Night source book and the other type of source books that list Vampire Clans, <br /> <br /> LW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3380-martian1912","name":"Martian1912","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T18:12:36-07:00","id":1488235,"title":"","content":"Some books through Renegade are traditional print. Those are the 'main' books: the core, Cam, Anarch, Sabbat, Second Inquisition and currently leftover stock of OPP's run of Cults and Chicago, and leftover stock of Modiphius' print of Fall of London. Renegade is going to be doing a reprint of Chicago and Cults with minor fixes (seems to just be grammar, typos, etc. rather than any kind of errata), and a reprint of Fall of London with errata (which it needs, Modiphius screwed the pooch with that book). If you go to Renegade's site and go into the Vampire directory, you can find links to all of them. You could also dig around on the internet on places like Amazon or online game shops for places selling their physical inventory of any of those as well.<br /> <br /> They haven't mentioned any prints of the OPP KS extra books. So all of those, you would have to get as Print on Demand from DriveThruRPG. That's going to be Chicago Folios, Let The Streets Run Red, Forbidden Religions, Trails of Ash and Bone, and Children of the Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https